# {{ project_name }}

A proto-driven Rust + Axum service deployable to **Databricks Apps**, scaffolded
with [trestle](https://github.com/open-lakehouse/trestle).

- Server: `crates/server` (Axum, generated routes)
- Shared models: `crates/common`
- HTTP client: `crates/client`
{% if with_frontend -%}
- Frontend: `frontend/` (React + Vite + TypeScript, generated TS client at `frontend/src/api`)
{%- endif %}

## Quickstart

```bash
# 1. Create the local composed environment (Envoy, storage, MLflow, ...)
#    with trestle env, then bring it up.
trestle env new {{ project_name | kebab_case }} --out-dir env
(cd env && docker compose up -d)

# 2. Generate code from .proto and run the app
just regen
just dev
```

See `trestle env list-modules --knobs` for the modules and per-module config,
and `trestle env render env` to re-render after editing `env/env.toml`.

## How the layout maps to Databricks

| Local | Databricks |
|-------|-----------|
| `cargo run -p {{ project_name | kebab_case }}-server` | `databricks bundle run {{ project_name | snake_case }}` |
| `http://localhost:${ENVOY_PORT}/api/2.0/mlflow/*` | `https://<workspace>/api/2.0/mlflow/*` |
| `X-Forwarded-Access-Token` (synthesized by Envoy) | `X-Forwarded-Access-Token` (OBO from Databricks Apps) |
| `DATABRICKS_HOST=http://localhost:${ENVOY_PORT}` | `DATABRICKS_HOST=https://<workspace>` |

The exact same code reads `DATABRICKS_HOST`, `DATABRICKS_TOKEN`, and the OBO
header. No env-conditional branches.

## Layout

```
{{ project_name | kebab_case }}/
├── Cargo.toml                  # workspace
├── trestle.yaml                # codegen config
├── buf.yaml + buf.gen.yaml     # proto build
├── proto/{{ project_name | snake_case }}/v1/    # source of truth
├── crates/
│   ├── common/                 # generated model types
│   ├── server/                 # Axum service (this is what Databricks runs)
│   └── client/                 # HTTP client + shared types
{%- if with_frontend %}
├── frontend/                   # React + Vite
{%- endif %}
├── app.yaml                    # Databricks Apps manifest
└── databricks.yml              # Databricks Asset Bundle
```

The composed local dev environment (Envoy, storage, MLflow, …) lives separately
under `env/`, created with `trestle env` — see the Quickstart above.

## Commands

```bash
just regen          # rebuild proto descriptor + regenerate Rust + TS
just dev            # cargo run + vite dev
just bundle-validate
just deploy         # databricks bundle deploy + run
just lint           # cargo clippy + buf lint + frontend lint
just test           # cargo test
```

